  "summary": {
    "intent": "Upgrade the oxc-react-docgen release workflow from callisto 0.8.0 to 0.10.0, get the PRs merged (using GitHub native stacked PRs), and get the first release PR opened.",
    "outcome": "PR #20 (callisto 0.10.0 pins, removed obsolete flags, callisto-validate fix) and #10 (comfy-table/crossterm) were merged as a native stack #21. The first release run failed on a disabled repo Actions setting; the user had the assistant enable it via gh, and release PR #22 (0.1.0 to 0.1.1) is now open and unmerged.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "The release workflow and ci.yml pin callisto actions by version. Upgrading needs every pin changed, including the `callisto-validate` action in ci.yml on main (8 refs at 0.8.0).",
        "callisto 0.9 removed `callisto validate`, `--profile production`, `--state` and `--recovery`. It made `--refresh-lockfiles` the default. 0.10.0 replaces validate with `callisto status --check` and fixes an E281 release-PR failure that 0.9.0 has.",
        "`callisto release --dry-run` plans 2 crates and 15 npm packages (5 owners plus 10 platform packages), with 0 artifact slots. Each npm owner's publish depends on its 5 platform packages.",
        "The repo's pre-commit hook runs the full lint suite, which floods command output. Check the commit and push results separately.",
        "AGENTS.md requires one line per paragraph in commit messages and PR bodies, why only, and no session links.",
        "Release PR creation needs the repo Actions setting `can_approve_pull_request_reviews=true`. The `orin-dx/callisto` repo has it on; this repo had it off. Callisto's docs don't mention it.",
        "`NPM_TOKEN` and `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` are org-level secrets visible to this repo. Only their names were checked, not their validity.",
        "PR #9 removed the `environment: release` reviewer gate, so merging the release PR publishes to crates.io and npm with no approval."
      ],
      "code": [],
      "workflow": [
        "`gh stack` (init, submit --auto, view, merge) supports native stacked PRs. `gh stack merge <n>` merges the whole stack atomically, so it is better than hand-retargeting PR bases and merging one at a time.",
        "`gh stack init` needs to check out the branches, so run it from a clean worktree when the main checkout has unrelated uncommitted changes.",
        "Check Actions settings and the state of `main` before a first end-to-end workflow run, not only the release branch. Missing `callisto validate` in ci.yml on main went unnoticed because only the release branch was checked.",
        "A subagent's commit message report is model output; review and adapt it to repo conventions before using it.",
        "Use `gh api -X PUT repos/.../actions/permissions/workflow` to change the Actions workflow permission settings."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "The CI Changesets job failed on #20 because ci.yml on main still used the removed `callisto validate`; the assistant had wrongly said nothing in the repo used it.",
      "The assistant told the user to merge the stacked PRs one at a time without checking that `gh stack merge` merges them together, and the user objected.",
      "The first Release & Publish run on main failed because Actions PR creation was disabled. It was flagged as unverified but not checked before merge.",
      "A transient GitHub API error hit the PR body update and needed a retry.",
      "The main checkout had unrelated uncommitted Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock changes (the tsc-client crate WIP), so the assistant had to work in extra worktrees.",
      "`gh stack view` showed a spurious 'needs rebase' warning on #20."
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "Decide whether to restore the `environment: release` reviewer gate before merging release PR #22, which triggers the first publish.",
      "Merge release PR #22 and watch the first end-to-end plan, build and execute run. `release execute` is resumable via `release_source_sha`.",
      "Optionally document the Actions PR-creation setting in the workflow header.",
      "Remove the leftover worktree `../oxc-stack` with `git worktree remove ../oxc-stack`.",
      "Dependabot may stop rebasing #10's branch because it was rewritten; #10 is already merged.",
      "The org-level Actions policy could not be inspected (missing `admin:org` scope)."
    ]
  },
